etwork adds another reliability layer with origin failover capability.\n\n**Performance Efficiency**: t3.medium instances provide 4x the capacity of t3.micro at 2x the cost, improving cost-efficiency while handling peak loads. ElastiCache dramatically reduces database queries for session data and metadata, cutting RDS load by an estimated 60-70%. CloudFront's 50% cache hit ratio reduces origin requests from 80M to 40M monthly. The architecture right-sizes compute resources—baseline traffic uses two instances at low utilization with burstable performance, while Auto Scaling adds capacity only during the 5 hours monthly of peak demand. Database upgrade to t3.medium provides adequate IOPS and connection capacity for the increased concurrent load.\n\n**Cost Optimization**: At $446.44 monthly, the architecture stays well within the $750 budget while handling 27x more requests than the original. Key optimizations include: burstable t3 instances for variable workload patterns; ElastiCache reducing RDS scaling needs by offloading read-heavy operations; CloudFront reducing origin bandwidth by 50%; single NAT Gateway (acceptable for this budget tier); right-sized RDS instance meeting performance needs without over-provisioning. Auto Scaling prevents paying for unused capacity during the 725 hours of normal traffic monthly. The cost structure aligns spending with actual demand.\n\n**Sustainability**: The architecture minimizes environmental impact through efficient resource utilization. Auto Scaling ensures compute resources are provisioned only when needed, reducing idle capacity during 99% of the month. ElastiCache and CloudFront caching reduce redundant computation and data transfer. Right-sized instances avoid over-provisioning. The use of managed services (RDS, ElastiCache, CloudFront) leverages AWS economies of scale for better energy efficiency than self-managed alternatives.",
